           optimize on a freshly constructed solver is a pure computation over the same LP inputs.
           Therefore two independent solver instances given the same objective/constraints/options
           must return the same objective value and point dimension when both calls succeed.
           A band-aid patch that merely suppresses the cycling symptom can still return a different
           solution on repeated fresh solves; this check catches that without relying on exceptions. */
        try {
